pra: 0172 - touch probe: read-only CYTT21403 bring-up behind pratouch=1

Rebased onto the landed 0171 GPU patch before landing: 0171 inserted
bsd/dev/prague_gpu.c after pra_charger.c in bsd/conf/files and
prague_gpu_probe() after pra_emmc_probe() in iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp,
which broke this draft's trailing context on both files (the touch
call-site hunk still applied clean, at offset 1). Both hunks rebased
minimally: the conf line still lands directly after pra_charger.c (the
charger is the driver this probe shares the bus with), with prague_gpu.c
now the first trailing context line; the extern still lands inside the
ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_PRA block, now after prague_gpu_probe(), with the
hunk rewritten to the standard symmetric 3-line context (the draft's
4-lead/3-trail shape trips GNU patch 2.8.1's --fuzz=0 matcher in this
duplicated #endif/#if PRA region even with byte-identical context).
Verified with GNU patch -p1 --fuzz=0 --dry-run on a freshly
reconstructed CI tree
(pristine xnu-8796.141.3 + the three dxb stage *.sh scripts + the full
0001-0171 stack via git apply, 164/164 applied, zero skips; before/after
transcripts in WORKLOG.md next to the draft).

What it does (all behind pratouch=1, default OFF - a boot without the arg
never maps a window and is byte-for-byte unaffected):

- bsd/dev/pra_touch.c: NEW read-only probe driver.
  - Maps /pra-touch ADT windows (reg[0] = i2c2 DesignWare host at
    0xFFD73000, reg[1] = pl061 gpio28 bank at 0xFFF1D000) and validates
    them against the dts values.
  - Reads COMP_VERSION/COMP_TYPE once (charger pattern; this host is
    proven live: COMP_VERSION=3132302a COMP_TYPE=44570140).
  - Dumps the gpio28 DAT/DIR slot of the touch IRQ line (gpio224 =
    gpio28.0, DAT at bank+0) and records the idle level.
  - One HID-over-I2C descriptor read at reg 0x0001 (16-bit LE register
    address, repeated-start read of 32 bytes) and prints the parsed
    identification (bcd, input/output/command/data registers, vid/pid/
    ver) exactly once. Known plan discrepancy: pra-touch-plan.md says
    28-byte descriptor; mainline cyttsp5.c (the protocol source the plan
    cites) reads and validates 32 bytes (struct + 4-byte reserved tail).
    This driver reads 32 and prints hid_desc_len raw either way.
  - Starts a 10 ms worker that polls the IRQ line, histograms both
    levels, reads the touch input register when the line differs from
    the probe-time idle level (polarity UNKNOWN, no assumption baked in)
    plus a 1 Hz heartbeat, decodes TT5 touch reports (mainline bit
    offsets: count = 5 bits @ bit16 from buffer+3 = bits[4:0] of byte[5];
    records at [7+10*i]; id/x/y/p at bits 8/16/32/48), and prints at
    most ONE line per 10 s with cumulative counters (reports/errs/
    corrupt) and the last contact. Errors back off 1 s. Every poll is a
    fixed-budget loop; no DMA, no interrupts, no gpio writes, no IC
    writes (descriptor + input-register reads only).
- bsd/conf/files + iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp: registered exactly like
  the charger (conf line after pra_charger.c; extern + boot-arg-gated
  call after the emmcprobe block in the PRA IOFindBSDRoot section).

Known hazard, documented in the driver header: the charger poll thread
reconfigures the SAME i2c2 controller every 10 s with no arbitration;
collisions corrupt one transaction on one side and both recover bounded.
Acceptable for a default-off probe; the shared pra_i2c layer (plan sketch
0162) is the first follow-up.

Testing requires appending pratouch=1 to the proven cmdline (never
shorten or reorder the 12 critical args) and the /pra-touch ADT node,
which lands as the tools/mkadt_pra.py edit in the same repo commit (CI
does not build tools/ - packaging regenerates adt-pra.bin).

